WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.835
Floyd Abrams is the doyen

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.803
of First Amendment law in America,

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.939
and he's joining me now from New York.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.407
Floyd Abrams, it's

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:09.109
great to have you on on this day

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:11.144
to to take us through this.

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:12.846
So from your perspective,

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:13.613
you know, essentially

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.315
defending the media.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.716
Is this a case

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.118
where justice has been done,

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:19.352
do you think?

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.123
I think justice has been done

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:26.693
in the broadest monetary sense

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.762
that we've ever seen, really

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:31.831
in any libel case in American history.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.401
Whether justice has been done

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:37.203
in the sense that the lesson

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.072
that Fox News

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.541
and perhaps others will learn

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:44.444
is to be not only more careful,

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:47.981
but simply not to engage in the sort of

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:51.017
of false editorializing

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:55.321
and putting people on who lie.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.458
You know, I can't say I'm that optimist

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:02.062
I take that that that will change much.

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.064
But I think that's at least

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:06.299
a waving red flag.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.268
What do you make of the fact that

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.869
and how did folks get away with

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.905
or is this de rigueur for settlement

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:15.241
not having to apologize on air

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.776
for its defamation?

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.778
And also, as you noted, in its statement,

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:19.946
it said that the

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:20.580
I believe it

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.648
said it acknowledges

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.850
that the judge found certain statements

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.151
about dominion to be false.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:26.252
Well, the judge said

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:29.122
every single statement that Fox News

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.957
reported about Dominion and

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.759
the election was false.

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.396
That's what the judge said.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:39.866
That is what is obviously true.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.902
The judge, in a written opinion,

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.904
made that very clear.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.840
In fact, he used capital letters.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.975
It is crystal clear.

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.110
He said that

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.177
all the statements

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:53.179
about Dominion were false.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.583
And so they were.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:57.984
Well,

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.686
it seems like a massive game of

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.521
chicken was being played.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.156
I mean, right down to the

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:04.357
to the last second

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.725
the jury had been seated.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.760
The opening arguments were due to start.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:08.962
You know, there'd been this delay

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.396
the day before.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:12.132
Well, you know, this the procedure.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:12.632
What do you think

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:15.869
was happening behind the scenes

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:17.370
talking or

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.273
talking about talking

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.143
Both sides had an interest

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.311
in disposing of the case.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.881
Fox's interest as obvious

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:30.450
because

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.318
it would have been,

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:35.421
at least in the broad public opinion,

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:38.791
ruinous in terms of how people,

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.627
not the Fox viewers,

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:43.796
But but how more people viewed Fox

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:46.366
as a propaganda outfit.

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.001
So there was a lot

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.236
a lot of reason for them to settle

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.771
The other reason was

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:53.773
I think they probably would have lost,

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.442
even though we have a legal system

00:02:56.843 --> 00:03:00.246
which is very sort of loaded, purposely

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.549
in favor of free speech,

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:04.551
which makes it very hard

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.719
to win a libel case like this.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.956
But this one was a very strong case

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.925
And then looking back on it,

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:14.294
certainly it's not surprising

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.563
that Fox would make every effort

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.698
to somehow put this behind it.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:19.832
And why do you think then

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.268
Dominion settled, you know?

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:24.938
Yeah, why?

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:29.242
Well, you know, Dominion is a business of

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.011
dominion is business

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.981
as not not litigation,

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.650
but but to make itself whole again,

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.921
no one's ever won or obtained

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:45.191
an amount like this.

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:48.194
If if there's anything that can be gained

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:50.630
by a libel case in the sense

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:53.099
that the public to the extent

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:54.867
the public followed this,

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.103
the public would know that

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.005
that that Fox had

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:02.075
erred or really worse than purposely

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:05.545
put false information on the air.

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:07.981
Dominion has done that.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:10.216
Whether the Fox viewers

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:14.821
will view Fox any less cordially

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:16.856
and in terms of inviting it

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.425
into their home, I rather doubt it.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.560
Let me ask you about

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.028
some of the tweets from Andrew Neil,

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.896
who used to be an insider.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.765
You know, he ran Murdoch's

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.300
Sunday Times here in the U.K.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.403
He ran Sky News at one point.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:31.804
And I spoke to him yesterday.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:32.305
Right

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:34.440
as we thought this trial was going ahead.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.408
After the settlement,

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:36.209
he tweeted

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:37.076
that it doesn't

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.312
end there for Rupert Murdoch.

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.114
Another voting machine company,

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:44.050
Smartmatic, is suing for 2.7 billion

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:46.286
with perhaps even a stronger case.

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:47.520
Plus, his shareholders

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.722
could sue him or Fox, the parent company,

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.257
for diminishing their assets.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.558
One already has.

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:54.027
And he goes on to say,

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.328
but it's already cost far,

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:56.796
far more than the U.K.

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.431
hatching hacking scandal

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:00.266
with much more financial exposure.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.301
Still to come

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.201
will strengthen

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:04.203
that part of the Murdoch family,

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.406
which wants to dump Fox News.

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:07.540
What do you make of that?

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.676
Do you think that. Yeah, go ahead.

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:11.177
No, know,

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:11.477
I'm sure

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:13.813
I think that's quite a prescient

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:15.682
observation.

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:18.451
It's all the things

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:20.019
on that list of statements

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.088
I think are accurate.

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:25.024
Yes, there certainly will be litigation

00:05:25.358 --> 00:05:27.794
by shareholder FOX.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.530
And yes, certainly

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.933
in terms of Fox's reputation

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:35.935
and whether

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:39.172
people at Fox on the financial side

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:41.341
will really want to continue

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:44.177
with Fox News, that that's a harder one.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.746
Certainly, Fox News is by far

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:49.682
the best known Fox product,

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.552
whether Fox,

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:54.754
whether the people who run Fox

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:58.324
will have found this all so distasteful

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:01.427
that that they'll even think about

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:04.030
divesting itself from Fox News

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:05.431
as a precedent.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:07.166
I don't think anybody has any idea.

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.901
But let's ask the bigger question.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:09.602
And Floyd Abrams,

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.070
you've been in the middle of this

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.472
for four decades.

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:14.540
You know, a free and independent press

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.175
in a democratic country is a

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:17.076
is a major

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:18.111
and important pillar

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:20.179
of a functioning democracy.

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:22.849
Do you think this trial has made that

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:25.051
more likely and less

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:29.422
or do we think that Fox and the attendant

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:30.123
even further

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:31.090
right wing

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.326
conspiracy theorists and all the others

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.962
will continue to get up to mischief

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:37.397
with their so-called

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:38.965
reporting or commentating

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:41.667
on the upcoming elections? Yeah,

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:43.069
look,

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:45.171
my judgment, my guess

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:48.708
is that Fox will not change

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:50.676
much.

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:54.013
My guess would be that, yes, they'll

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:56.315
they'll send instructions down,

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:57.316
you know, don't do this

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:58.217
sort of thing again.

00:06:58.217 --> 00:06:58.618
We don't

00:06:58.618 --> 00:07:00.319
we don't need this trouble

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.422
and this enormous

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:04.590
amount of money being being paid out.

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:07.860
But in terms of whether Fox will change

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.963
what I'll call editorial policy, we'll

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:13.900
well move it all off towards the center

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.970
or even to caring more about avoiding

00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:20.840
the correct charge of propaganda.

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:23.443
One can't tell.

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:26.212
My guess is I'm afraid now

00:07:26.913 --> 00:07:28.614
you say the correct charge of propaganda.

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:29.415
That's interesting.

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:31.083
Dominion lawyer Justin Nelson,

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:33.286
after the settlement said this to CNN.

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:34.587
Take a listen.

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:37.557
I do hope that this really does

00:07:37.557 --> 00:07:38.891
send a message

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:41.060
that it is so, so important

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.428
to tell the truth

00:07:42.428 --> 00:07:43.930
and that if you don't tell

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:45.998
the truth, lies have consequences.

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:47.667
And I think this is what it established.

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:48.968
And that is why

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:50.203
there is accountability today.

00:07:50.203 --> 00:07:52.371
There's accountability to dominion

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:54.240
and there's accountability to democracy.

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:56.476
So, Floyd Abrams, we

00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:57.310
discussed a little bit

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.912
the other side of that question is

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:02.748
how does this, in the bigger picture,

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:04.484
potentially change

00:08:04.484 --> 00:08:05.384
the decades

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:07.820
old New York Times versus Sullivan

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:09.722
of 1964

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:12.458
which established a very, very high bar

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:14.093
for libel and defamation

00:08:14.093 --> 00:08:15.595
it's almost impossible

00:08:15.595 --> 00:08:16.929
for media companies

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:18.531
to lose in these cases.

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:20.566
Do you think in the future

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:22.668
either the Supreme Court or elsewhere

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:26.372
that law, that precedent will be changed?

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:28.307
Well, first,

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:29.642
I don't think it will be changed

00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:31.878
because of the result.

00:08:31.878 --> 00:08:34.213
The settlement in this case

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:36.082
As for whether it will be changed

00:08:36.082 --> 00:08:38.851
because we've had a change of membership

00:08:38.851 --> 00:08:40.720
on our Supreme Court

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.154
that is more possible

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:44.323
now than it had been in the past.

00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:46.859
Two members of the court have already

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:49.962
in writing urged that it be changed.

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:51.631
And there's reason to think

00:08:51.631 --> 00:08:53.833
that there are more

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:55.968
that would be if I had to guess,

00:08:56.235 --> 00:08:56.936
I would say

00:08:56.936 --> 00:08:58.671
it will not change

00:08:58.671 --> 00:09:00.373
in the foreseeable future.

00:09:00.373 --> 00:09:02.975
I don't think that five of our nine

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:03.776
Supreme Court

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:07.380
justices are going to be prepared to say

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:11.217
that this precedent from 1964,

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:15.254
which certainly in general has served us

00:09:15.254 --> 00:09:19.725
well as a freedom protecting body of law.

00:09:20.126 --> 00:09:20.927
I don't think that

00:09:20.927 --> 00:09:22.395
there are going to be five votes

00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:24.030
but I may be,

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:25.798
as they say, whistling Dixie.

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:27.967
So finally, let me ask

00:09:27.967 --> 00:09:28.935
you from your decades

00:09:28.935 --> 00:09:31.103
and decades of experience in this.

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:33.873
What feeling do you have right now.

00:09:33.973 --> 00:09:34.740
You know

00:09:34.907 --> 00:09:36.809
you started many many years ago

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:38.844
defending the press as well as many other

00:09:38.844 --> 00:09:40.846
you know, corporate cases.

00:09:40.846 --> 00:09:41.948
You've taken all the rest of it.

00:09:41.948 --> 00:09:44.250
But what's your feeling now

00:09:44.584 --> 00:09:46.385
looking back at history

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:48.554
and to the future?

00:09:50.356 --> 00:09:52.658
It was very important, in my view,

00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:53.826
for Fox

00:09:53.826 --> 00:09:54.594
and one way

00:09:54.594 --> 00:09:56.762
or the other to lose this case.

00:09:57.363 --> 00:09:59.832
For one thing, New York Times versus

00:09:59.832 --> 00:10:03.336
Sullivan is not an impenetrable barrier

00:10:03.736 --> 00:10:06.572
to plaintiffs with very good cases

00:10:06.806 --> 00:10:07.239
winning.

00:10:07.239 --> 00:10:09.909
I think, as I'll bet Fox thought

00:10:10.309 --> 00:10:12.478
that there was a very good chance

00:10:12.478 --> 00:10:14.347
Fox would lose this case

00:10:14.347 --> 00:10:15.781
had it gone to the jury.

00:10:15.781 --> 00:10:17.817
I think it's more likely than not

00:10:17.817 --> 00:10:19.819
that that would have happened

00:10:19.819 --> 00:10:21.721
in terms of the impact

00:10:21.721 --> 00:10:24.090
really on democracy.

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.191
I think we're better off

00:10:25.191 --> 00:10:27.293
for having had this case.

00:10:27.293 --> 00:10:29.495
I think it does send a message

00:10:29.495 --> 00:10:31.163
I think it is a warning,

00:10:31.163 --> 00:10:34.433
at least to the sort of entities

00:10:34.433 --> 00:10:35.568
that would be prepared

00:10:35.568 --> 00:10:38.471
to engage in the worst excesses

00:10:38.904 --> 00:10:41.674
of of the worst of journalism,

00:10:42.341 --> 00:10:46.112
to be careful that that it is not a

00:10:46.112 --> 00:10:48.214
get out of jail free card

00:10:48.214 --> 00:10:50.049
that the Supreme Court has given.

00:10:50.049 --> 00:10:53.019
It's just very, very hard to win

00:10:53.019 --> 00:10:54.954
a libel case here

00:10:54.954 --> 00:10:56.656
brought by a public figure.

00:10:56.656 --> 00:10:57.657
And it should be.

